---@meta
-- Generated by `fengine --write-api`; do not edit.

--- A world position or vector; `{1, 2, 3}` also works. Positions need x and z; offsets and directions may leave components out (0). Components are within -1000000 to 1000000.
---@alias Vec3 {x: number, y?: number, z: number}

--- A grid cell: 0-based integer coordinates, layer 0 by default. `{x, z, layer}` positionally also works; cell tables the engine returns carry more fields, which are ignored.
---@alias Cell {x: integer, z: integer, layer?: integer}

--- A rectangle in canvas or image pixels; `{x, y, w, h}` positionally also works.
---@alias Rect {x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number}

--- 0xRRGGBBAA, a color name or '#rrggbb[aa]', or 0..1 components (above 1 is HDR where supported). A plain number is always 0xRRGGBBAA, so 0.5 is an error.
---@alias Color integer|string|{r: number, g: number, b: number, a?: number}|number[]

--- Text layout and style: `size` is 0 to 1024 (0 = the font's own), `width` (0 to 1000000) wraps (0 = no wrapping), `visible` reveals that many units (typewriter).
---@alias TextOptions {font?: string, size?: number, color?: Color, width?: number, align?: 'left'|'center'|'right', visible?: integer, shadow?: Color, outline?: Color, line_gap?: number}

